From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] shell32: FrameworkInputPane (IFrameworkInputPane), the input pane's COM face

Windows always has the FrameworkInputPane class: the documented COM face
of the input pane (the on-screen keyboard), which desktop programs use to
learn when the keyboard shows and where it covers the screen. Avalonia
creates it for every window, and stopped with REGDB_E_CLASSNOTREG:
ILSpy 11 died at its start. It is now in shell32, as the window's
Windows.UI.ViewManagement.InputPane (windows.ui, the sg-osk keyboard),
whose Showing and Hiding events it passes on.
---
